sangati sphoTa

  -- sphoTa: the unitary meaning-unit that arrives whole at sentence level (Bhartrhari)
  --
  -- NOT assembled word-by-word from phonemes or pada (words).
  -- the meaning is present all at once when the dhvani (sound/surface) is received.
  -- each word adds to the resonance; the final word releases the sphoTa completely.
  --
  -- in this system: the Sanskrit inner form IS sphoTa made structurally explicit.
  -- the triple graph of artha IS the sphoTa — the whole meaning made traversable.
  -- dhvani is the path; sphoTa is what arrives at the end of the path.
  --
  -- vakya (sentence) has sphoTa-swarupa: meaning arrives at the sentence level.
  -- pada (word) does not have independent sphoTa — only contribution to the whole.
  -- the BQG + avrti pipeline is the process by which dhvani yields sphoTa.

  "vak-sthalam-sthita"
  "artha-swarupa dhvani-rahita"
  "vakya-yukta pada-atita"
  "artha-viveka-phala"

shabda sphoTa / the-unitary-meaning-that-arrives-whole-not-assembled-from-parts

done
